    {
      "executionState": "enabled",
      "id": "note",
      "kind": "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "# Orbital Bloom · Flight through a growing light tunnel\nThe opening petal sculpture holds briefly, then the camera accelerates into its dark center. Each crown and its orbiting comets lives at a fixed depth: it grows past the camera while another colored crown emerges at the vanishing point. Six repeating depth slices keep the tunnel supplied with new forms. A half-float feedback texture carries older light forward and twists it into trails. The final pass adds stars, a violet nebula, faint speed rays, and the core corona. Everything is procedural and seeded; no external assets are needed. Trail, Sparkle, Orbit speed, Nebula, and Travel speed tune the effect; changing them restarts the GPU simulation. OrbitalBloom.metal sits beside this workflow through the Source File port. Image Output saves each completed 1440 × 900 frame as PNG; Stop Loop to finish."
      },
      "resources": {},
      "title": "How Orbital Bloom works"
    },
    {
      "executionState": "enabled",
